// ─── array.tr ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Prelude placeholder for array UFCS helpers (STRING_UFCS_OPERATOR_CHAR_RFC.md
// §5.3/§7 step 6).
//
// Deliberately near-empty: a genuinely useful array utility library (sum,
// map, filter, etc.) needs to work across every element type, which means
// generic free functions (`fn<T> sum(arr: T[]): T`) -- but UFCS resolution
// was deliberately scoped to NON-generic candidates only (RFC step 4,
// TypeChecker::tryUFCSFallback()'s receiver matching is a plain, non-generic
// exact-name match). Writing separate concrete overloads per element type
// isn't a real substitute for a generic array library. This file exists so
// `array` is a valid prelude module name today; real content is blocked on
// UFCS gaining generic-function support, a separate future step.
